Z||000000||87ECO5||06-01-2000||03:26 PM||||I thought there was a thread started recently that discussed the steps required to change the fluid in the manual transaxle.  I ran a few searches but couldn't find anything.  I also checked my Haynes manual but they only dicuss the steps for the automatic transaxle fluid.<P>Can someone help me?  TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||87ECO5||06-02-2000||07:26 AM||||Anyone?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||06-02-2000||07:51 AM||||You have to crack it open at the bellhousing, and allow the fluid to seep out from what I've heard. Since there is no drain plug for the Izuzu.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||06-02-2000||12:06 PM||||Wow! crack the bell?  I guess mine isn't an Isuzu.  I suppose it's a Muncie 4spd. because there's a drain plug on this one.(1986)Good luck man.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||LarryB||06-02-2000||12:22 PM||||The drain plug on the Isuzu is on the lower side below the drivers-side axle. You don't have to crack open the bellhousing. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>You have to crack it open at the bellhousing, and allow the fluid to seep out from what I've heard. Since there is no drain plug for the Izuzu.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
